    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Toss the ribs with salt, flour and a little white vinegar. Add water, rub gently, then rinse away the flour and drain.",
        "timestampSeconds": 51
      },
      {
        "text": "Place the ribs in cold water with scallions, ginger and cooking wine. Bring to a boil over medium-low heat, skim the foam, then boil for another 1–2 minutes.",
        "timestampSeconds": 130
      },
      {
        "text": "Lift out the ribs, rinse in warm water and drain.",
        "timestampSeconds": 176
      },
      {
        "text": "Put the ribs in a clean pan with 3 ginger slices, a scallion section, star anise, dried chilies, beer, light soy sauce, dark soy sauce, oyster sauce and sweet bean sauce. Add water to cover.",
        "timestampSeconds": 223
      },
      {
        "text": "Cover, bring to a boil, then reduce to low heat and simmer for 1 1/2 hours until tender.",
        "timestampSeconds": 264
      },
      {
        "text": "Remove the aromatics during simmering once they have released their flavor. When the ribs are tender, uncover and turn up the heat to reduce the sauce until thick.",
        "timestampSeconds": 267
      },
      {
        "text": "Plate the ribs, spoon over the sauce and garnish with chopped scallions.",
